        "id": "p46-q11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the number of bacteria at 40 minutes.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "4000 bacteria.",
          "worked": "At $n=40$, the graph gives $y=4000$. There are 4000 bacteria.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p46-q11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "The number of bacteria can be modelled by $A\\times b^n$ where $A$ and $b$ are constants.\n\nUse guess and check to find, to two decimal places, an upper and lower estimate for the value of $b$. The upper and lower estimates must differ by 0.01.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1.03<b<1.04$.",
          "worked": "Initially, $A=1000$. At 40 minutes, the graph gives 4000 bacteria, so we need $1000b^{40}\\approx4000$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\n1000(1.03)^{40}&\\approx3262<4000\\\\\n1000(1.04)^{40}&\\approx4801>4000\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nHence the lower estimate is 1.03 and the upper estimate is 1.04: $1.03<b<1.04$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ],
